# Arch Angel — a Strong enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 8/12 Strong enemies — 22 life, bribe 100 gold
# enemy: Arch Angel (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0221.dck "Arch Angel (Wh, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 11 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 12 lines (56
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/arch_angel.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 8)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/arch_angel.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Strong) — "Arch Angel" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Arch Angel
22 Plains
2 Mana Vault
4 Wrath of God
4 Soul Net
4 Mishra's Factory
4 The Hive
4 Serra Angel
4 Onulet
4 Osai Vultures
4 Tetravus
4 Swords to Plowshares
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vBlack  3 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vBlue   3 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vGreen  3 Swords to Plowshares
#   .vRed    3 Reverse Damage
#   .vWhite  3 Disenchant
SB: 3 Reverse Damage
SB: 3 Disenchant
